WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.300 --> 00:00:02.567
-Oh, my gosh.
-Is that the fastest --

00:00:02.567 --> 00:00:05.234
That's the fastest wardrobe
change I've ever had on a show.

00:00:05.234 --> 00:00:06.834
-You are fantastic
and a stunner.

00:00:06.834 --> 00:00:08.534
-I'm a professional at it,
actually.

00:00:08.534 --> 00:00:10.534
-Yeah, you are actually.
You're really good.

00:00:10.534 --> 00:00:13.200
-Quick changes. Very good.
-Can I just say -- Look at this.

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:14.801
Stunning.
-Oh, thank you.

00:00:14.801 --> 00:00:16.367
-On the cover of "Vogue."
This is --

00:00:16.367 --> 00:00:18.834
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:18.834 --> 00:00:21.734
You've done over 35 covers
of "Vogue."

00:00:21.734 --> 00:00:23.234
-It's crazy.
-How does it feel?

00:00:23.234 --> 00:00:24.667
Does it --
-I don't even know.

00:00:24.667 --> 00:00:28.167
It's, like, I mean, obviously
an honor and amazing,

00:00:28.167 --> 00:00:30.501
but I don't know
how it went by so fast.

00:00:30.501 --> 00:00:32.567
It's, like, I remember each one,

00:00:32.567 --> 00:00:36.734
like, such a vivid memory
of the day with so many people

00:00:36.734 --> 00:00:39.467
that are involved and work
so hard to create each photo.

00:00:39.467 --> 00:00:42.701
So it's amazing
that it's been that many.

00:00:42.701 --> 00:00:44.767
-I have a photo of you.

00:00:44.767 --> 00:00:48.767
This is your first photo
that I think was in "Vogue."

00:00:48.767 --> 00:00:50.667
Is this possible?
-Oh, I actually --

00:00:50.667 --> 00:00:52.367
-No?
-That's a funny story.

00:00:52.367 --> 00:00:55.667
So, I didn't know
what magazine this was in.

00:00:55.667 --> 00:00:59.234
I just know my mom had a tear
sheet from it growing up.

00:00:59.234 --> 00:01:01.000
And I didn't really know
the story behind it.

00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:03.968
And last -- It's a picture of me
on vacation with my family.

00:01:03.968 --> 00:01:07.167
I was holding an Eiffel Tower
I just bought

00:01:07.167 --> 00:01:09.767
and my little film camera.

00:01:09.767 --> 00:01:13.234
And then I saw a photo shoot
going on here,

00:01:13.234 --> 00:01:15.834
and I went and stand
in front of the photographer.

00:01:15.834 --> 00:01:17.100
See, I'm very interested.

00:01:17.100 --> 00:01:18.567
-Yeah, you're like,
"I want to be in the shot."

00:01:18.567 --> 00:01:20.267
-And he took a picture.
I was in the shot.

00:01:20.267 --> 00:01:21.667
This was in some
French magazine.

00:01:21.667 --> 00:01:23.434
And I didn't know the story
behind it.

00:01:23.434 --> 00:01:25.567
And then a couple of years ago,
I posted it.

00:01:25.567 --> 00:01:26.834
See? Here's my post.
-Yeah.

00:01:26.834 --> 00:01:29.501
-"Does anyone know
who shot this editorial?

00:01:29.501 --> 00:01:31.901
If anyone can recall. Surreal."

00:01:31.901 --> 00:01:37.267
And a photographer that I've
been working with since 2014

00:01:37.267 --> 00:01:39.534
at this point was like,

00:01:39.534 --> 00:01:42.634
"Gigi, I took that photo
how many years ago."

00:01:42.634 --> 00:01:45.067
And now I work with him now
backstage at shows.

00:01:45.067 --> 00:01:46.434
-And he had no idea
who you were.

00:01:46.434 --> 00:01:49.334
-No idea that he shot me.
No idea we had that connection.

00:01:49.334 --> 00:01:51.267
And I know him now as an adult.
It's wild.

00:01:51.267 --> 00:01:53.267
-Isn't that cool?
-Yeah, it's really crazy.

00:01:53.267 --> 00:01:54.868
-You start off as just a kid

00:01:54.868 --> 00:01:56.100
walking around
with an Eiffel Tower,

00:01:56.100 --> 00:01:58.334
and then you end up
on the cover of "Vogue."

00:01:58.334 --> 00:02:00.067
What are the stickers,
by the way?

00:02:00.067 --> 00:02:01.200
-Those stickers are --

00:02:01.200 --> 00:02:03.234
So, this is
"Vogue: Netherlands."

00:02:03.234 --> 00:02:06.767
My mom's Dutch, so I was
really excited to do this cover,

00:02:06.767 --> 00:02:09.200
and I did it with one of my
best friends, Alana O'Herlihy.

00:02:09.200 --> 00:02:11.801
And we got to really
creative-direct this shoot

00:02:11.801 --> 00:02:13.133
and have a lot of fun with it.

00:02:13.133 --> 00:02:14.501
So, these stickers are actually

00:02:14.501 --> 00:02:17.934
from a Dutch amusement park
called The Efteling.

00:02:17.934 --> 00:02:21.334
And it's a beautiful, kind of
quaint amusement park

00:02:21.334 --> 00:02:23.868
in a forest with all these,
like, fairy tales.

00:02:23.868 --> 00:02:25.234
And these stickers,

00:02:25.234 --> 00:02:28.367
they were flown from Holland
for this shoot.

00:02:28.367 --> 00:02:30.968
-You used to go to this park?
-Yes, when I was a kid.

00:02:30.968 --> 00:02:32.868
Every summer with --

00:02:32.868 --> 00:02:34.501
My aunt and uncle
live across the street.

00:02:34.501 --> 00:02:35.868
They had, like, yearly passes.

00:02:35.868 --> 00:02:38.634
And it's just
a really special place to me,

00:02:38.634 --> 00:02:42.434
and I kind of wanted
to nod to all those memories

00:02:42.434 --> 00:02:45.067
and my oma, who passed away.

00:02:45.067 --> 00:02:46.834
But we had
really special times there,

00:02:46.834 --> 00:02:48.767
and that's, you know,
for all the Dutchies.

00:02:48.767 --> 00:02:50.367
They'll get that, for sure,
when they see it.

00:02:50.367 --> 00:02:52.167
-I love that.
Congratulations on doing that.

00:02:52.167 --> 00:02:53.701
I think it's cool
that you did that.

00:02:53.701 --> 00:02:55.334
You do some things where I go,

00:02:55.334 --> 00:02:56.801
"Man, Gigi,
don't do these things."

00:02:56.801 --> 00:02:58.267
Because you scare me.
-What are they?

00:02:58.267 --> 00:03:00.567
-Well, there are photos that
you take that are dangerous.

00:03:00.567 --> 00:03:02.567
-Let's see it.
-I'm gonna show you one.

00:03:02.567 --> 00:03:04.801
Here's you on a scaffolding.
Are you kidding me?

00:03:04.801 --> 00:03:05.834
-Oh, yeah.
-No!

00:03:05.834 --> 00:03:07.334
-Yeah.

00:03:07.334 --> 00:03:10.133
-The answer is,
"Gigi can't do it. Sorry."

00:03:10.133 --> 00:03:12.534
-I'm asked to do
a lot of crazy things.

00:03:12.534 --> 00:03:14.300
And, yeah, it just happens.

00:03:14.300 --> 00:03:16.300
But my management
and my security,

00:03:16.300 --> 00:03:19.267
they always get these calls
from some production teams

00:03:19.267 --> 00:03:20.868
that are like --
They're panicking.

00:03:20.868 --> 00:03:23.067
They're like, "So we're maybe
gonna have to have Gigi

00:03:23.067 --> 00:03:25.934
on a 100-foot thing
hanging in the sky.

00:03:25.934 --> 00:03:28.434
Will she do it? If not,
we'll have these options."

00:03:28.434 --> 00:03:30.133
I don't say no.
I say yes to everything.

00:03:30.133 --> 00:03:32.033
-No. Absolutely not.
-I'm insane. I do it all.

00:03:32.033 --> 00:03:33.834
-=That's why you need me
as your manager --

00:03:33.834 --> 00:03:35.501
to get in there so you don't --

00:03:35.501 --> 00:03:37.667
-No, they tell them like,
"Gigi will go for it."

00:03:37.667 --> 00:03:39.267
So, yeah, I always say yes.

00:03:39.267 --> 00:03:41.000
-Here's you on the same
scaffolding shoot.

00:03:41.000 --> 00:03:42.834
-In the beginning, it's scary,
but then by the end of it...

00:03:42.834 --> 00:03:46.033
-You're dancing. Jumping on it.
What's wrong with you?

00:03:46.033 --> 00:03:48.133
-I'm in a harness.
I'm in a harness. See?

00:03:48.133 --> 00:03:49.934
-No. Either way,
it's still scary.

00:03:49.934 --> 00:03:51.367
-It's movie magic.
-It's still scary.

00:03:51.367 --> 00:03:53.801
-And stunting.
-[ Laughs ] Stunting.

00:03:53.801 --> 00:03:55.467
Can we talk about
"Next in Fashion"? Okay.

00:03:55.467 --> 00:03:58.000
-I'm wearing this outfit,
so clearly,

00:03:58.000 --> 00:03:59.267
I'm trying to talk about
"Next in Fashion."

00:03:59.267 --> 00:04:00.901
-Yes. You're always
the next in fashion.

00:04:00.901 --> 00:04:02.934
-Thank you.
-You're cohosting this

00:04:02.934 --> 00:04:05.701
with Tan France,
who we love, from "Queer Eye."

00:04:05.701 --> 00:04:07.534
-Yes. We love.
-How do you know Tan?

00:04:07.534 --> 00:04:09.534
Before the show,
did you know him or no?

00:04:09.534 --> 00:04:12.000
-So, I,
like the rest of America,

00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:13.834
five years ago --
or the world --

00:04:13.834 --> 00:04:16.267
when "Queer Eye" came out,
I was a huge fan.

00:04:16.267 --> 00:04:17.767
Fell in love with them...

00:04:17.767 --> 00:04:21.434
and was, like, going through
a breakup or something,

00:04:21.434 --> 00:04:23.400
like, sitting on my couch
all weekend

00:04:23.400 --> 00:04:25.968
near when the show aired.

00:04:25.968 --> 00:04:28.100
You know, crying, laughing
all day watching them.

00:04:28.100 --> 00:04:29.434
And they just, like,
made my week.

00:04:29.434 --> 00:04:32.801
And I saw that Eva Chen,
head of instagram Fashion,

00:04:32.801 --> 00:04:34.367
had them in her office --

00:04:34.367 --> 00:04:36.667
or had Tan in her office,
specifically.

00:04:36.667 --> 00:04:39.267
And I was like, "I'm going to
have to FaceTime him."

00:04:39.267 --> 00:04:41.100
So, I FaceTime him. We talk.

00:04:41.100 --> 00:04:42.868
And I'm like --
This never happens, by the way.

00:04:42.868 --> 00:04:44.968
Like, I'm obsessed with Jimmy.

00:04:44.968 --> 00:04:47.868
Like, I consider him one of my
favorite people in the world.

00:04:47.868 --> 00:04:50.734
And, like, I was never, like,
a weirdo in this way.

00:04:50.734 --> 00:04:53.033
But with Tan for some reason,
I'm like, "Will you come

00:04:53.033 --> 00:04:54.767
to my house and have tea
with me right now?"

00:04:54.767 --> 00:04:57.434
-Yeah, you've never
invited me over for tea.

00:04:57.434 --> 00:05:00.100
-I know! But that's, like,
out of, like --

00:05:00.100 --> 00:05:02.234
I'm not trying to, like,
annoy you, you know?

00:05:02.234 --> 00:05:05.667
Like, you're clearly busy.
-You would never annoy me.

00:05:05.667 --> 00:05:07.434
-So is Tan.
But you know what I'm saying.

00:05:07.434 --> 00:05:11.100
-So you call -- you FaceTime
the "Queer Eye" guys.

00:05:11.100 --> 00:05:12.667
-So I FaceTime them
and I'm like,

00:05:12.667 --> 00:05:14.000
"Do you want to be my friends?"

00:05:14.000 --> 00:05:15.567
Pretty much like,
"Please come over."

00:05:15.567 --> 00:05:17.234
And we -- They came over.

00:05:17.234 --> 00:05:19.934
We, like, had lunch at my house.
We, like, talked, hung out.

00:05:19.934 --> 00:05:22.667
It was Antoni, Tan,
and Jonathan that day.

00:05:22.667 --> 00:05:25.934
And now Antoni is one of
my best friends, my neighbor.

00:05:25.934 --> 00:05:27.968
And obviously,
Tan and I are doing the show.

00:05:27.968 --> 00:05:30.133
And it's just, like,
such a special experience.

00:05:30.133 --> 00:05:32.501
-Are you loving doing this show?
Because I know you.

00:05:32.501 --> 00:05:35.133
You've been a great guest
on the show and a good friend.

00:05:35.133 --> 00:05:38.200
But I know that you love
reality competition shows.

00:05:38.200 --> 00:05:39.901
-Big fan.
-We've talked about this. Yes.

00:05:39.901 --> 00:05:41.367
There was one
you kept telling me.

00:05:41.367 --> 00:05:42.968
There was, like, a glass-blowing
show that you loved.

00:05:42.968 --> 00:05:45.300
-Oh, I love glass blowing.
I love "LEGO Masters."

00:05:45.300 --> 00:05:47.067
-"LEGO Masters" is good, too.

00:05:47.067 --> 00:05:49.467
-Yeah. Like, all of them --
obsessed.

00:05:49.467 --> 00:05:51.601
But, now, do you like
hosting and judging?

00:05:51.601 --> 00:05:53.868
-Love hosting, love judging.

00:05:53.868 --> 00:05:56.901
Such a special,
you know, new experience for me,

00:05:56.901 --> 00:06:00.434
getting to go to the same studio
every day with the same crew.

00:06:00.434 --> 00:06:02.601
You know, it's like
an office job, like you.

00:06:02.601 --> 00:06:04.734
And, um --

00:06:04.734 --> 00:06:06.667
[ Laughter ]

00:06:06.667 --> 00:06:08.267
I'm just trying to be you,
Jimmy.

00:06:08.267 --> 00:06:10.300
Okay, so, but anyways --
-It's a good thing.

00:06:10.300 --> 00:06:12.601
-No, it's the best.
It's such a nice feeling.

00:06:12.601 --> 00:06:14.567
-You're a natural.

00:06:14.567 --> 00:06:16.234
You're also --
Not only are you stunning,

00:06:16.234 --> 00:06:18.801
but you're also
funny and charming

00:06:18.801 --> 00:06:21.734
and interested
in things and people,

00:06:21.734 --> 00:06:24.467
and you're a good host.
-And normally, like, in my job,

00:06:24.467 --> 00:06:28.934
I think I haven't been
really ever given the time

00:06:28.934 --> 00:06:31.968
and the space to, like,
really open up and show myself.

00:06:31.968 --> 00:06:34.300
Not on purpose,
for my fashion job.

00:06:34.300 --> 00:06:38.367
It's just such a small,
you know, snippet of time

00:06:38.367 --> 00:06:41.601
that you're given in those
kind of fashion, more --

00:06:41.601 --> 00:06:43.734
-You get to be you.
-Yeah, I get to be me.

00:06:43.734 --> 00:06:46.067
And I think I try to be funny.

00:06:46.067 --> 00:06:47.667
-Yeah, you are.
-You guys judge for yourself.

00:06:47.667 --> 00:06:49.067
-I want to show everyone a clip.

00:06:49.067 --> 00:06:50.601
Here's Gigi Hadid
in "next in Fashion."

00:06:50.601 --> 00:06:51.868
Take a look at this.

00:06:51.868 --> 00:06:53.000
-Gi?
-Yeah?

00:06:53.000 --> 00:06:54.133
-You want to tell me
how you're feeling?

00:06:54.133 --> 00:06:57.567
Should we start with --
Diandre. Thoughts?

00:06:57.567 --> 00:07:00.434
-It's really cool. I think
the proportions are spot on.

00:07:00.434 --> 00:07:02.467
-Does it feel royal?
-I think it does feel royal.

00:07:02.467 --> 00:07:05.000
I think it's hip-hop royalty
for sure.

00:07:05.000 --> 00:07:06.501
-Agreed, agreed. Okay.

00:07:06.501 --> 00:07:08.968
Megan. It's definitely bold.

00:07:08.968 --> 00:07:10.934
And I've got a feeling
a lot of people

00:07:10.934 --> 00:07:12.634
are either going to
love it or hate, but --

00:07:12.634 --> 00:07:14.334
-That's what I want.
-That's exactly what we want.

00:07:14.334 --> 00:07:17.100
-I love this jacket.
I think it's really cool.

00:07:17.100 --> 00:07:19.667
So I'm going to be happy
just if it gets done.

00:07:19.667 --> 00:07:22.367
-James, I hate to say,
might be in trouble.

00:07:22.367 --> 00:07:24.968
-Royal is here, and James is
here, and his look is here.

00:07:24.968 --> 00:07:27.033
And he needs to bring
both of those here.

00:07:27.033 --> 00:07:30.267
-That's exactly right.
He's here. Bring it in here.

00:07:30.267 --> 00:07:31.567
Gigi Hadid!

00:07:31.567 --> 00:07:34.200
"Next in Fashion"
premieres Friday on Netflix.

00:07:34.200 --> 00:07:36.434
Chase Stokes joins us
after the break.

00:07:36.434 --> 00:07:37.968
Stick around, everybody.

